course: dictionary
lesson: 1500
title: Ce: this, it, and CE
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Ce» is a French word that means «this», «that» or «it». It sounds like «suh». It comes before a noun, as in «ce livre», which means this book. The word changes its form to fit the noun: «cet» comes before a word starting with a vowel, «cette» is used for a girl-type noun, and «ces» is for more than one.
explain: In French, «c'est» joins «ce» and «est» and means «it is». On the Brittany beach, a French kid says «C'est un crabe !», which means it is a crab. Then «Qu'est-ce que c'est ?» asks what it is. Notice that the word «ce» is in all three.
explain: CE is an English abbreviation, and it is not French. It stands for «Common Era», the same years as AD. «Paper was made in China by about 100 CE» means around the year 100 in the Common Era. BCE means «Before the Common Era», so it marks years before the start of that count.
explain: On toys and electrical goods, a CE mark means the item meets European safety rules. Look for it on a charger or a toy. Always check the context: is the word in a French sentence or a history or safety one? That tells you which meaning you need.
fact: «Ce» means «this» or «that» or «it» in French.
fact: «C'est» means «it is» in French. It sounds like «say».
fact: «Qu'est-ce que c'est ?» means «what is it?»
fact: CE stands for «Common Era», and it is used with years, such as «around 600 CE».
fact: BCE means «Before the Common Era». A CE mark on a toy shows it meets European safety rules.
exercise: In French, «ce livre» means what in English? | a green cat | *this book | the moon | three books
exercise: «Chess began in India around 600 CE.» What does CE stand for? | Christmas Eve | Before the Common Era | *Common Era | Crown Estate
exercise: A CE mark on a toy shows what? | It means the toy is very old | It means the toy was made in Paris | It means the toy can float | *It meets European safety rules
test: «Qu'est-ce que c'est ?» means what? | Where is the beach? | *What is it? | How old are you? | Who is that?
test: What does BCE mean? | Basic Common Essentials | Born in Common England | *Before the Common Era | Beyond the Common Era
exam: In «C'est un crabe !», what does c'est mean? | *it is | the sea | you are | a crab
